      "summary": "Cardrona Alpine Resort is open for skiing today, with no fresh snowfall overnight but classic spring conditions across the mountain, firm underfoot early before softening quickly. It's currently 1°C with winds around 37 km/h gusting to 64 km/h, under a mostly cloudy sky with a chance of afternoon showers; the natural snow base sits at 112 cm. The Kindy Conveyor, Learner Conveyors, Valley View and T-Bar are running on schedule, while McDougall's Chondola and Whitestar Express are on wind hold, with Captains Express, Soho Express, Willow's Quad and Wells Pipe Platter delayed; 4 of 10 lifts are currently running. The Olympic Halfpipe is closed today for the Snow League event. (Issued: 7:30am, 19 Sep) There's no sightseeing today with the gondola-linked McDougall's lift not running; the access road is chain-free but chains must be carried, with an active road hazard advisory in place. Lifts & terrain Lifts Open 4 / 10 Runs Open 0 / 38 Percent open 0 %",
