      "summary": "Treble Cone is open for skiing today, with the front that moved through overnight clearing the skies and leaving soft, groomed spring snow across the mountain. It's currently 2°C with winds around 32 km/h gusting to 58 km/h; the natural snow base at the top of Home Basin sits at 150 cm, with no fresh snowfall in the past 24 hours. Home Basin Express, Saddle Quad and the Beginner Platter are all running on schedule, all 3 of 3 lifts open; Home Basin, Powder Bowl, Saddle Basin, Summit Slopes and the terrain park are all running, with only Matukituki Basin and Motatapu Chutes on hold. Home Basin opens at 8:30am and Saddle Basin at 9am today. (Issued: 7:30am, 19 Sep) Backcountry and skinning access are both open; the access road is chain-free but chains must always be carried, with an active road hazard advisory and a free shuttle running from the bottom of the access road. Lifts & terrain Lifts Open 3 / 3 Runs Open 0 / 59 Percent open 0 %",
